            <ArticleTitle>Breaking the pain contract: A better controlled-substance agreement for patients on chronic opioid therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>827-835</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3949/ccjm.83a.15172</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>&quot;Pain contracts&quot; for patients receiving long-term opioid therapy, though well-intentioned, often stigmatize the patient and erode trust between patient and physician. This article discusses how to improve these agreements to promote adherence, safety, trust, and shared decision-making.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2016 Cleveland Clinic.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
